# Introduction {#ch:intro}

This chapter states the problem; @ch:methods gives the model and the
experiment. The sensitivity of the fitted model is summarised in
@fig:sens, and panel @fig:sens-b is the one a grower should read first.
The fitting procedure is @alg:bisect, its driver is @lst:dine, the
measurements are in @tbl:yield, and the model itself is @eq:mass.
@sec:model derives it.

## Scope {#sec:scope}

The study covers one cultivar and one region.

![A hazel tree, at half its natural size.](tree.png){#fig:tree scale=0.5}

@fig:tree shows the tree the measurements were taken from.

# Methods {#ch:methods}

## The model {#sec:model}

The model is stated in @eq:mass and fitted by @alg:bisect.

$$
E = mc^2
$$ {#eq:mass}

::::{figure #fig:sens caption="Sensitivity of the fitted model" columns=2}

:::{subfigure #fig:sens-a caption="Temperature"}
![](panel.png)
:::

:::{subfigure #fig:sens-b}
![](panel.png)
